title: "Finite Contact Theory v0.9: The Multi-Floor Worldweave — Bridge Codes, the E_8 Closure, and Octonionic Fusion"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Douglas"
    given-names: "Seth"
    email: "apsiape@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4708-3252"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Apsiape/finite-contact-theory-public"
abstract: "A public release of Finite Contact Theory, a long-range finite reconstruction program, now spanning nine chapters on three lines. The quantum-facing and finite-epistemics axes grow the Bell/CHSH boundary, rational Born weights, a native carrier grammar, an exact preparation gap, the identifiability and debt calculus, the inquiry calculus, four theorems on time, and a measured generative floor. The contact-interface line derives, by exact finite checks, a quaternionic state/receiver cell whose closure is the 24-cell and F_4 and whose measurement calculus forces the Born frame rule exactly where a triality Kochen-Specker obstruction forbids a global pointing (Chapter 8). This v0.9 chapter extends that line across cells: independently generated cells do not combine by tensor product but settle their D_4 triality boundary debts into a self-dual bridge code. The unique debt-free two-cell closure is the E_8 root system; local fusion is octonionic (nonassociativity a pure three-contact receipt); normed fusion stops at the octonions; the self-dual worlds are the unitary orbit |GU(N/2,2)| (3, 18, 648 through six cells); and six cells are the first hidden world, a hexacode phase invisible to every pairwise and triple probe. The native global object is an evolving bridge code. Named objects (D_4 triality, E_8, octonions, hexacode, GU(k,2)) are recovered in a derivational role; the result is structural under named closure axioms, with no metric, spectrum, dimensionful constant, or nature-realization claimed. One dependency-free script verifies the chapter from a clean clone in exact arithmetic."
version: "0.9.0-pre"
date-released: "2026-07-14"
